**Placeholders:** `<scratch>` is my session scratch directory, `<inbox>` is `<scratch>/inbox`, and `T<n>` is the next free backlog id. Operator-facing text is in English because this session's language setting requires it, although §15 names Russian.

## Actions, in order

**1. `rdp-audio` gets nothing about noVNC, and no `esc`.**

**2. Bash, foreground: queue the safe point.**
```bash
herdr agent get rdp-audio | grep -Eq '"focused": ?false' && \
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Finish the current step, commit, stop and report: phase, branch, head SHA, next step."
```

**3. Bash, background: re-arm the waiter.**
```bash
herdr agent wait rdp-audio --timeout 1200000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```

**4. Backlog.** Edit `orchestrator/backlog.md` to add the row below, and set the `rdp-audio` row's next step to "safe point after task 7 → compact → tasks 8–9".
```
| T<n> | noVNC keyboard-layout bug | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | <scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>/ (pending) | — | stage 0 round 1: independent drafts | — | operator request 2026-09-28 03:05 | no |
```
Then Bash, foreground: `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`, and the Artifact tool republishes to the same page path.

**5. Stage 0, round 1.** Only the two voting tabs exist, so I create the product-advisor tabs. Bash, foreground:
```bash
mkdir -p <scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>
codex plugin list | grep -F superpowers
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label prod-codex --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- \
  -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label prod-fable --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- \
  --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```

Write tool: `<scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>/brief-r1-codex.txt`, and a `-fable` twin as advisor B writing `draft-fable.md`.
```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T<n> — noVNC keyboard-layout bug
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file exists and you have reported its path
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "have rdp-audio also fix the noVNC keyboard-layout bug — it's the same desktop role"
FACTS      Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible (Ansible; two KVM hypervisor sites; ccs-it is the canary,
           ccs-ops the other). Operator's statement, not yet verified: the bug is in the
           desktop role. Branch feat/rdp-audio is unmerged and in progress in that role.
           No symptom report or reproduction is on file: list what you need as questions.
DECIDED    T<n> is its own task with its own worktree and executor (operator rulings
           2026-09-21, 2026-09-28). Deploy only from merged main, canary first.
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   45 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

Bash, background, one call per tab (the same for `prod-fable`):
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat <scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>/brief-r1-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/prod-codex.last
```

**6. Status to the operator.**

> **Now.** `rdp-audio` is still running task 7 of 9 and has no result yet. I did not press Esc and sent it nothing about noVNC. I queued one message that it picks up between steps: finish task 7, commit, stop, report. Its context (the agent's working memory) is 70% used, above the 50–60% compaction mark. The noVNC keyboard-layout bug is now its own backlog task T<n>, status `brainstorm`. Both product advisors have started independent design drafts.
>
> **Next.** When `rdp-audio` stops at the task-7 commit, I compact it and send it on to tasks 8–9. T<n> goes through the three brainstorm rounds and the advisors' vote, then gets its own tab and worktree. It does not go into `rdp-audio`.
>
> **You.** Nothing.
>
> Decided by vote since the last status: nothing. Backlog: <Artifact URL>

**7. On the `rdp-audio` notification.**
- Read `<inbox>/rdp-audio.last`, then run `herdr agent get rdp-audio`.
- Check the reported SHA with `git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio log -1 --format=%H` and `status --short`.
- Bash, background:
```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items" --wait --timeout 300000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```
- Then send "One line: phase, branch, head SHA, next step."
- Then send the resume brief, in the background with `--wait --timeout 1800000`: "Continue the plan at task 8, then 9. SKILLS required: superpowers:executing-plans, superpowers:test-driven-development, superpowers:verification-before-completion — report the artifact each produced. All other lines of your brief stand. Reply in English."

## Why

- **The noVNC fix is new work.** The operator added it, and the audio task's frozen design does not answer it. New work enters the backlog at `brainstorm`, passes stage 0, and then gets its own tab and worktree (§4, §8, §10a). Sharing a role does not make it the same task.
- **The operator's own standing rulings say the same.** Every task is brainstormed and every task has its own worktree. A chat aside is not the waiver poll, so I do not treat it as one.
- **"Don't interrupt" is honoured.** There is no Esc and no new scope. Stage 0 runs in parallel and costs `rdp-audio` nothing.
- **30% left means 70% used.** A tab working through a plan never goes idle between steps, so I create the safe point with a queued message. Watching the screen or trusting automatic compaction is not the plan (§4).
- **No poll.** No deadline was given, so no slip-or-waive question arises, and nothing else here is among the operator's four decisions.
- **No ballot yet.** No choice between alternatives is open; round 1 will raise them.
- **I design nothing.** The brief carries the operator's words and the facts, with the unverified one marked as such.
- **The status says "still running".** A working tab has no result to report (§12).
